  "notes": "Represents the 'IT field' request \u2014 the general 'Information Sciences and Technology, B.S.' major (ISSWC_BS) was tried first but turned out to have no University Park Suggested Academic Plan (effectively World-Campus-only / not currently offered at any campus), so this major was substituted: it has a real, current, University Park-based 4-year plan. 'Application Focus Selection' slots (9 credits across 3 terms) are chosen from a College-approved list not enumerated in the bulletin's course table. 'etm' marks the courses everything else in the sequence assumes are done. UPDATE after the prereq-parser fix: both STAT 200 and its SCM 200 alternate require MATH 21 (which needs MATH 4, which needs MATH 3), none of which were anywhere in this plan -- added the MATH 3 -> MATH 4 -> MATH 21 chain explicitly (front of Semesters 1-3), same fix as the 2026 plan. Also dropped the generic, unenumerated 3cr 'Elective' slot (Semester 8) to partially offset the 9 new credits. FLAGGED FOR HUMAN REVIEW (same as 2026): even after that offset, this plan cannot be packed into exactly 8 real terms under the simulator's greedy scheduler -- a real consequence of the newly-correct STAT 200 prereq chain, not a data error. HANDBOOK VERIFICATION PASS (real archived bulletin, bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2025-2026/.../cybersecurity-analytics-operations-bs/, matching the CYAOP_BS 2025-26 curriculum flowchart PDF at ist.psu.edu/assets/uploads/documents/CYBER-Flowchart.pdf): wired all 3 'Application Focus Selection' slots with a 'match' regex built from this catalog year's real 7-track list -- Application Development is now HCDD/IST cross-listed (HCDD 311/IST 311 etc.) instead of IST-only, and Entrepreneurship adds ENGR 310. Same convention/caveats as the 2022 fix above.",
